  "legacy_defects": [
    "the org.md write reports the character count as `bytes`: ten 'é' answer bytes 10, where UTF-8 holds 20 (docket org-admin-orgmd-put-reports-characters-as-bytes)",
    "disk delete reports an unlink failure with the raw OSError text, which carries the host's Windows path, to an admin and a kiosk visitor alike (the disk download route reduces host paths for visitors) (same docket)"
  ],
  "scope": "Legacy boundary of the org administration routes (P01 F7) on disposable SQLite. Hub, net, sandbox, container and docker calls are spies; the WSL command runner is a recorded fake and a mounted org disk a temp folder; the routes, the ledger, the store's create and delete, the defaults file, the workspace files and the host folders the sweep removes are real. Legacy conformance evidence only: not a runtime census, not PostgreSQL or Rust qualification."
}
